Spec: Repository Bootstrap

Platform: Bash/Spec Kit 1.0.10/SpecDD CLI

Purpose:
  Reproduce the tested development toolchain and install the bridge through the same thin component installer used to prove local and immutable-archive packaging.

Owns:
  ./bootstrap.sh
  ./install.sh

References:
  ../integration/specdd/extension.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/workflow-overlay.sdd
  ../integration/specdd-preset/specdd-preset.sdd

Must:
  Bootstrap pins Spec Kit `1.0.10` and SpecDD framework `1.5`, and records upstream SpecDD CLI `1.1.1` as the current stable baseline.
  Until stable upstream SpecDD exposes typed intended-target resolution equivalent to the bridge contract, bootstrap installs the temporary resolver provider from `https://github.com/dmos62/specdd-cli.git` branch `feature/resolve-intended-targets`.
  Temporary resolver-provider validation requires package version `1.2.0` and resolver support for `--file`, `--folder`, and `--sdd-file`.
  Resolver capability, not package-version identity, determines bridge intended-target behavior outside bootstrap installation checks.
  The temporary resolver provider is removable once a stable upstream SpecDD CLI passes the focused typed intended-target parity tests.
  The active Spec Kit integration is `codex` so extension and preset commands can be registered under tested Spec Kit `1.0.10`.
  Existing initialized repositories change active integration through supported Spec Kit integration commands.
  ./install.sh installs the extension, preset, and project workflow overlay through supported Spec Kit lifecycle commands.
  ./install.sh accepts the local checkout, a local archive, or an immutable GitHub tag, commit, or release archive as installation source.
  Remote installation rejects mutable GitHub branch archives.
  ./install.sh supports clean bridge removal, reinstall, and installation-health checks.
  Bootstrap delegates bridge materialization to ./install.sh after establishing the pinned development toolchain.
  Check mode verifies bridge command materialization, preset augmentation materialization, lifecycle hook registration, workflow-overlay resolution, and `specdd lint` without changing repository state.
  Missing required host executables report dependency-specific remediation before bootstrap mutates repository state.

Must not:
  Patch generated Spec Kit commands, installed extension state, installed preset state, workflow-overlay state, or SpecDD framework files directly.
  Use npm, PyPI, or a public Spec Kit catalog as the bridge distribution requirement.

Done when:
  Bootstrap apply followed by check succeeds with the tested Spec Kit baseline, temporary typed intended-target provider, bridge, and structural workflow gates available through the active Codex integration.
  Local checkout installation and immutable GitHub archive installation use the same native Spec Kit component operations.
